Title: Add MentionControl notification filters
Body:
Supersedes #4744 with unused language callbacks removed and settings registration inlined.

## Changes

Added separate mute switches for everyone/here, direct mentions, DMs, replies, and roles. Muted messages are automatically marked as read. Each account starts with every switch off.

Marking a message read also reads earlier messages in that channel. This does not scan old history or hide every badge globally. The adapter currently targets Discord Stable 649389; other builds retain native behavior.

## Demo

User-provided direct-mention before/after example:

![Direct-mention before/after example](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/OwaisByte/Vencord/db2a5234549057c562098022cb6161e86c7b7a9b/mention-control-direct-mentions-before-after.gif)

Settings:

![MentionControl settings](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/OwaisByte/Vencord/db2a5234549057c562098022cb6161e86c7b7a9b/mention-control-settings.png)

## Validation

- `pnpm test` and `pnpm buildWeb`
- 121 offline behavioral tests
- 13 settings interaction checks; no account actions or acknowledgements during rendering/settings changes

The GIF demonstrates direct-mention badge behavior, not all five categories or audio delivery.

## Related work

[ReadAllNotificationsButton](https://github.com/Vendicated/Vencord/pull/217) and [OnePingPerDM settings](https://github.com/Vendicated/Vencord/pull/1802) informed the API and presentation review. Their bulk-read and sound-only behavior were not copied into this plugin.

Made with OpenAI Codex and I checked the code.

