Title: Preserve help option groups when flags conflict
Body:
When an application option shadows one of the help option's flags, `Help.visibleOptions()` creates a replacement option for the remaining flag. It copies the description but drops `helpGroupHeading`, so the help option moves to `Options:` and its configured group can disappear.

For example:

```js
const program = new Command()
  .option('-h, --host <host>')
  .addHelpOption(
    new Option('-h, --help', 'display help').helpGroup('Information:')
  );
console.log(program.helpInformation());
```

Before this change, `--help` appears under `Options:`. After the change it appears under `Information:` as configured.

Preserve the group when creating the replacement option for either a short-flag or long-flag conflict. Two regression tests cover explicit `Option.helpGroup()` and `Command.optionsGroup()` configuration; both fail before the fix.

Suggested changelog: Preserve the help option's group when a conflicting flag is hidden.

Validation:
